---
[`zml.Buffer`](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/zml/buffer.zig)
holds backend handles for a concrete tensor. Create the inputs on the platform
used to compile your executable. The `io` argument is a `std.Io`, and
`allocator` is a `std.mem.Allocator`. A return type with `!` can carry an error.

# [Create device buffers]($heading.id('buffer'))

- `zml.Buffer.fromSlice(io, platform, slice)`\
  `!Buffer`. Copy a `zml.Slice` from host memory and wait for transfer.
- `zml.Buffer.fromBytes(io, platform, shape, bytes)`\
  `!Buffer`. Copy host bytes using the supplied `Shape`. The bytes must match its element type and size.

# [Inspect the shape and wait for transfers]($heading.id('shape-and-readiness'))

- `buffer.shape()`\
  `Shape`. Read the buffer's metadata.
- `buffer.await(io)`\
  `!void`. Wait for the backend buffer to become ready.

When using `fromSliceOpts` or `fromBytesOpts` with `.wait = false`, keep the
source bytes alive and unchanged until `buffer.await(io)` completes successfully.

# [Read back to host memory]($heading.id('read-back-to-host-memory'))

- `buffer.getValue(T, io)`\
  `!T`. Read back into a host type with matching representation and byte size. It copies bytes without converting the element type.
- `buffer.toSliceAlloc(allocator, io)`\
  `!Slice`. Read back into an owned host slice. Release it with `slice.free(allocator)`.

# [Release the buffer]($heading.id('release-the-buffer'))

- `buffer.deinit()`\
  `void`. Release the buffer through a mutable handle.

See [Load and inspect model weights]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/load-and-inspect-model-weights')) for an example of loading weights into device buffers.
